<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nevryuy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1252</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nevryuy was a Mongol commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> who in 1252 led a punitive expedition into north-eastern Rus' against Grand Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrei-ii-of-vladimir">Andrei Yaroslavich</a> of Vladimir. His army defeated Andrei near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pereslavl-zalessky">Pereslavl-Zalessky</a> and ravaged the area, and Andrei fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. The campaign, known as Nevryuy's raid, allowed Andrei's brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a> to receive the grand principality from the Horde.</p></div>
